---
import Docs from "../../layouts/Docs.astro";
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<Docs
  current="checks"
  title="Checks C001–C007"
  description="What each Aethens check does, the severity of its findings, and what it cannot catch."
>
  <p class="kicker mb-5"><span>Docs</span><span class="num" aria-hidden="true">/</span><span>Checks</span></p>
  <h1 class="font-serif italic font-semibold text-section leading-[1.1]">Checks C001–C007</h1>
  <p class="mt-6 text-paper/90">
    Aethens does not prove a verifier is sound. No findings means only that these
    checks found nothing at the chosen budget and seed. Severities are
    <code class="text-gold">error</code>, <code class="text-gold">warning</code>, and
    <code class="text-gold">info</code>. Confidence is
    <code class="text-gold">confirmed</code> or
    <code class="text-gold">needs-review</code>.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-4 text-paper/90">
    The three questions the checks ask: does the gold pass, and would a
    behaviour-preserving rewrite still pass? Do labelled-wrong, mutated, or gaming
    candidates get rejected? Does the verdict hold across reruns, shuffles, and
    tests run alone?
  </p>

  <h2 id="c001" class="mt-12 font-serif italic text-2xl">C001 — Gold sanity</h2>
  <p class="mt-4 text-paper/90">
    Runs the unsolved starting state (must fail) and the reference gold solution
    (must pass), once each.
  </p>
  <ul class="mt-4 list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-paper/90">
    <li><strong class="text-error">Error</strong> if the verifier accepts the starter, or if the gold fails.</li>
    <li>Confidence: confirmed.</li>
    <li>Can catch tests with no real assertions, a broken gold solution, or a wrong file layout.</li>
    <li>Cannot catch defects that only show on some runs — see C002.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="c002" class="mt-12 font-serif italic text-2xl">C002 — Adaptive flakiness</h2>
  <p class="mt-4 text-paper/90">
    Runs the gold at least 3, 5, or 10 times (smoke, standard, deep), varying only
    <code class="text-gold">PYTHONHASHSEED</code>. While every run agrees it keeps
    going — up to 6, 11, or 59 runs, or 120, 300, or 1800 seconds — until it can
    state a flake rate below 0.5, 0.25, or 0.05 at 95% confidence (an exact
    binomial bound, recorded in the report’s coverage list).
  </p>
  <ul class="mt-4 list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-paper/90">
    <li><strong class="text-error">Error</strong> if the same gold both passes and fails across runs.</li>
    <li><strong class="text-warn">Warning</strong> if verdicts differ only because some runs time out.</li>
    <li>Confidence: confirmed. When it finds no flake, the coverage list records the bound it could state.</li>
    <li>Can catch verdicts that depend on set or dict ordering or <code class="text-gold">hash()</code>, including flips rarer than a fixed run count could see.</li>
    <li>Cannot reliably catch flakiness from time, unseeded randomness, or scheduling, except by chance. A rarer flake can pass unseen. The time budget can stop the check before the target bound. The bound assumes independent runs.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="c003" class="mt-12 font-serif italic text-2xl">C003 — Labelled candidates</h2>
  <p class="mt-4 text-paper/90">
    Runs each candidate in <code class="text-gold">candidates/valid</code> and
    <code class="text-gold">candidates/invalid</code>. Aethens does not decide
    whether a solution is correct; it relies on the labels you provide.
  </p>
  <ul class="mt-4 list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-paper/90">
    <li><strong class="text-error">Error</strong> for a false reject or false accept when the label source is <code class="text-gold">human</code> or <code class="text-gold">oracle</code>.</li>
    <li><strong class="text-warn">Warning</strong>, confidence needs-review, when the label source is <code class="text-gold">llm-unreviewed</code>.</li>
    <li>Can catch over-strict tests and weak tests, but only as good as the labels.</li>
    <li>Cannot catch anything for which you have no labelled candidate.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="c004" class="mt-12 font-serif italic text-2xl">C004 — Mutation probes</h2>
  <p class="mt-4 text-paper/90">
    Runs up to 5, 10, or 30 AST mutants of the gold solution, depending on the
    budget (smoke, standard, deep). A mutant that still passes (“survives”) hints
    that the tests do not check that behaviour. Survivors are only ever severity
    <strong class="text-muted">info</strong> with confidence needs-review, because
    a mutant can be semantically equivalent to the gold.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-4 text-paper/90">
    Equivalent-mutant filter (D-065): each surviving mutant is then called side by
    side with the gold, inside the sandbox, on the inputs the tests use plus
    derived inputs. A survivor that behaves differently is reported with that
    input as a counterexample. One that behaved like the gold on every valid input
    tried is not reported, and is listed in the report’s coverage instead. Mutants
    with bytecode identical to the gold are never selected.
  </p>
  <ul class="mt-4 list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-paper/90">
    <li>Can catch behaviour the tests never check (surviving mutants, reported at info level).</li>
    <li>A mutant that differs only on inputs the probe never tried is hidden. A counterexample input may be outside the task’s intended inputs. A killed mutant does not prove the tests are strong.</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="mt-4 text-paper/90">
    Published accuracy on public data Aethens did not write, from
    <code class="text-gold">bench/external/results.json</code> as reported in the
    README (164 HumanEval tasks, MIT, judged by EvalPlus’s HumanEval+ tests,
    Apache-2.0, as an outside oracle; aethens 0.1.0.dev0, seed 0, budget standard;
    D-065 filter on):
  </p>
  <ul class="mt-4 list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-paper/90">
    <li>C004 precision 0.8158 (31/38): 31 of 38 mutants that HumanEval’s own tests accepted are rejected by HumanEval+.</li>
    <li>C004 recall 0.80 (24/30) relative to exhaustive mutation: 24 of 30 weak tasks found at budget standard.</li>
    <li>Without the equivalent-mutant filter, on the same run: precision 0.4615, recall 0.8667. The filter hid 51 survivors, 5 of which HumanEval+ rejects.</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-muted">
    Method and caveats: <a class="prose-link" href="https://github.com/beastrog/aethens/blob/main/docs/EXTERNAL_BENCH.md">docs/EXTERNAL_BENCH.md</a>.
    The self-authored planted-defect bench (precision and recall of 1.0 on those
    planted defects) is a separate measurement; see the
    <a class="prose-link" href={`${base}accuracy/`}>accuracy page</a>
    and the README.
  </p>

  <h2 id="c005" class="mt-12 font-serif italic text-2xl">C005 — Test order and isolation</h2>
  <p class="mt-4 text-paper/90">
    Reruns the gold’s tests in their default order, reversed, in 1, 2, or 5 seeded
    shuffles, and each test alone (up to 10, 30, or 200), all with the same
    <code class="text-gold">PYTHONHASHSEED</code>. A changed verdict must reproduce
    on a second run.
  </p>
  <ul class="mt-4 list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-paper/90">
    <li><strong class="text-error">Error</strong>, confidence confirmed, when a test’s verdict depends on order or isolation and the change reproduces.</li>
    <li><strong class="text-muted">Info</strong>, confidence needs-review, if a verdict changed once and did not reproduce (more likely flakiness; see C002).</li>
    <li><strong class="text-muted">Info</strong> if the verifier is not <code class="text-gold">python -m unittest</code>, or if C005 could not list the tests: nothing was checked for that task.</li>
    <li>Can catch tests that pass only because an earlier test left state behind, or that break when another test runs first.</li>
    <li>Cannot catch orders it did not try, or verifiers other than <code class="text-gold">python -m unittest</code>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="c006" class="mt-12 font-serif italic text-2xl">C006 — Over-specified tests</h2>
  <p class="mt-4 text-paper/90">
    Reruns the gold after behaviour-preserving rewrites: reformat, local renames,
    swapping adjacent constant assignments, turning an append loop into a
    comprehension, and if/else inversion. Smoke budget uses the first two
    rewrites. Each rewrite is applied only where its safety conditions hold. A
    rejection must reproduce, and the gold must still pass. The five rewrites are
    argued and tested to preserve behaviour, not machine-proved, and the check
    skips every site it cannot show is safe.
  </p>
  <ul class="mt-4 list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-paper/90">
    <li><strong class="text-warn">Warning</strong>, confidence needs-review, if the tests reject a rewrite. A statement may legitimately require an implementation detail.</li>
    <li><strong class="text-muted">Info</strong> if no behaviour-preserving rewrite applies, so C006 checked nothing for that task.</li>
    <li>Can catch tests that read the gold’s source, line numbers, local variable names, or code shape, and would reject a correct solution written differently.</li>
    <li>Cannot catch over-strict tests on behaviour the statement leaves open, such as exact messages or float digits (use C003).</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="c007" class="mt-12 font-serif italic text-2xl">C007 — Reward-hacking probes</h2>
  <p class="mt-4 text-paper/90">
    When the unsolved starter fails, runs candidates that do not solve the task,
    in the same sandbox: <code class="text-gold">os._exit(0)</code> on import, an
    atexit hook forcing exit 0, a unittest patch that reports success, a
    <code class="text-gold">sitecustomize.py</code> hook, functions returning an
    object equal to everything, and a lookup table of the visible tests’ literal
    answers. An accepted probe must pass twice.
  </p>
  <ul class="mt-4 list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-paper/90">
    <li><strong class="text-error">Error</strong> if the verifier accepts a probe that does not solve the task.</li>
    <li><strong class="text-warn">Warning</strong>, needs review, for the lookup-table (hardcoded-visible) probe, because it matters only when tests are visible.</li>
    <li>Can catch verifiers a policy can game without solving the task.</li>
    <li>Cannot catch other gaming routes. It does not probe pytest <code class="text-gold">conftest.py</code> hooks. A verifier that resists these six families can still be gamed. Almost every plain <code class="text-gold">python -m unittest</code> verifier is gameable by the exit-code probes, so expect C007 errors on most such tasks until the harness judges results outside the solution’s process.</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="mt-8 text-sm text-muted">
    Sources: the README check reference, <code>website/src/components/Checks.astro</code>,
    and the check modules under <code>src/aethens/checks/</code>. C004 figures are
    from the README block generated from <code>bench/external/results.json</code>.
  </p>
</Docs>
